<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juozas Ambrazevičius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903–1974</span> · Also known as Juozas Brazaitis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juozas Ambrazevičius was a Lithuanian literary scholar who served as acting prime minister of the Provisional Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> in June to August 1941, after the uprising against Soviet rule at the start of the German invasion. The Germans dissolved the government, and he later emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, where he wrote under the name Juozas Brazaitis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juozas-ambrazevicius.jpg" alt="Juozas Ambrazevičius" width="320" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotoateljė „Modern“ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juozas_Ambrazevi%C4%8Dius-Brazaitis_(retouched).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
